        "original_id": "8ec19d94-06a1-5ff4-979a-e58e2aee7778",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Courtney Love, Steven Baigelman, Keanu Reeves, Vincent D'Onofrio, Cameron Diaz, Tuesday Weld, Dan Aykroyd, Delroy Lindo, Dave Callahan, Paul Clark, Andy Golding, Andy Bolton, Frank Stebbing\n- Organizations: Hole, The Wolfhounds\n- Places: Romford, UK\n- Products: Feeling Minnesota\n- Topics: alternative rock, indie pop, noise pop, crime drama comedy film\n\nFacts:\n- The Wolfhounds are an indie pop and noise pop band formed in Romford, UK, in 1985 by Dave Callahan, Paul Clark, Andy Golding, Andy Bolton, and Frank Stebbing.\n- The Wolfhounds were originally active until 1990.\n- Courtney Love was born as Courtney Michelle Harrison on July 9, 1964.\n- Courtney Love is an American singer, songwriter, actress, and visual artist.\n- Courtney Love formed the alternative rock band Hole in 1989 and rose to prominence as its frontwoman.\n- Feeling Minnesota is a 1996 American crime drama comedy film written and directed by Steven Baigelman.\n- Feeling Minnesota stars Keanu Reeves, Vincent D'Onofrio, Cameron Diaz, Tuesday Weld, Dan Aykroyd, Delroy Lindo, and Courtney Love.",
